<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01E6">Remark <span data-tag="01E6">4.5.1.19</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor between $\infty $-categories. If $F$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories, then the induced map of cores $F^{\simeq }: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\simeq } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}^{\simeq }$ is a homotopy equivalence of Kan complexes. This follows from Corollary <a data-tag="01DV" href="/tag/01DV">4.5.1.6</a> (and Remark <a data-tag="01DW" href="/tag/01DW">4.5.1.7</a>): if the isomorphism class $[F]$ is an invertible morphism in the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}$, then the homotopy class $[ F^{\simeq } ]$ is an invertible morphism in the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$. </p>
